@startuml
title Vue Déploiement — BrokerX (État initial: Monolith → Étape 2a: LB/Cache → Étape 2b: Gateway/Microservices)

/' 
NOTE IMPORTANTE: 
- **État initial** = Monolith REST avec UC-01/02 implémentés (avant Phase 2)
- **Étape 2a + 2b** = Phase 2 du projet (Observabilité + LB + Cache + Gateway + Microservices)
- **Phase 2** = Correction actuelle (énoncé fourni par le professeur)
- **Phase 3** = Prochaine correction (après livraison Phase 2)
- Les 2 étapes de Phase 2 sont séparées visuellement pour faciliter l'implémentation progressive

Énoncé Phase 2 : "Industrialisation de l'observabilité et de la performance (tests de charge, 
load balancing, caching) + évolution vers architecture microservices orchestrée par API Gateway"
'/

' =======================
' ÉTAT INITIAL: Monolith simple (Avant Phase 2)
' =======================
package "État initial: Monolith (Avant Phase 2 - UC-01/02 ✅)" {
  node "VM de démo / Docker Compose" as phase1 {
    node "container: BrokerX API\n(.NET 9)" as app1 {
      component "REST API v1" as api1
      component "Signup (UC-01)" as signup1
      component "Auth (UC-02)" as auth1
      component "Deposits (UC-03)" as deposit1
    }
    database "MySQL\n(port 3306)" as db1
    
    node "Simulateurs locaux" {
      component "otp-sim" as otp1
      component "kyc-sim" as kyc1
      component "pay-sim" as pay1
    }
  }
}

' =======================
' ÉTAPE 2a: LB + Cache + Observabilité (Phase 2 du projet - partie 1)
' =======================
package "Étape 2a: Load Balancing & Observabilité (Phase 2 énoncé - À implémenter)" {
  node "Docker Compose étendu" as phase2 {
    node "NGINX\n(Load Balancer)" as nginx {
      component "Reverse Proxy" as proxy
      component "Round-robin LB" as lb
    }
    
    node "BrokerX API × N instances" {
      node "app-1" as app2_1
      node "app-2" as app2_2
      node "app-3" as app2_3
      node "app-4" as app2_4
    }
    
    node "Redis\n(Cache)" as redis {
      component "Cache pour:\n- /portfolio\n- /market-data\n- /reports" as cache
    }
    
    node "Observabilité" {
      component "Prometheus\n(Metrics)" as prom
      component "Grafana\n(Dashboards)" as grafana
      component "k6\n(Load Tests)" as k6_tool
    }
    
    database "MySQL" as db2
  }
}

' =======================
' ÉTAPE 2b: API Gateway + Microservices (Phase 2 du projet - partie 2)
' =======================
package "Étape 2b: API Gateway & Microservices (Phase 2 énoncé - À implémenter)" {
  node "Architecture distribuée" as phase3 {
    node "KrakenD\n(API Gateway)" as krakend {
      component "Routage" as route
      component "Auth/CORS" as gw_auth
      component "Rate Limiting" as throttle
    }
    
    node "Microservices" {
      component "Identity Service\n(UC-01, UC-02)" as identity_svc
      component "Wallet Service\n(UC-03)" as wallet_svc
      component "Market Data Service\n(UC-04)" as marketdata_svc
      component "Orders Service\n(UC-05)" as orders_svc
      component "Reporting Service" as report_svc
    }
    
    node "NGINX\n(per-service LB)" as nginx3
    
    database "MySQL\n(SHARED)\nport 3307" as db_shared {
      note right
        Base unique partagée:
        - identity_db
        - wallet_db
        - orders_db
        - marketdata_db
        - reporting_db
      end note
    }
    
    node "Simulateurs" {
      component "market-feed-sim" as mkt_sim
      component "otp-sim" as otp3
      component "kyc-sim" as kyc3
      component "pay-sim" as pay3
    }
    
    node "Redis Cluster" as redis3
    node "Prometheus" as prom3
    node "Grafana" as grafana3
  }
}

' =======================
' Connexions Phase 1
' =======================
api1 --> db1 : EF Core
api1 --> otp1 : HTTP
api1 --> kyc1 : HTTP
api1 --> pay1 : HTTP

' =======================
' Connexions Phase 2
' =======================
nginx --> app2_1 : HTTP/1.1
nginx --> app2_2 : HTTP/1.1
nginx --> app2_3 : HTTP/1.1
nginx --> app2_4 : HTTP/1.1

app2_1 --> db2 : EF Core
app2_2 --> db2 : EF Core
app2_3 --> db2 : EF Core
app2_4 --> db2 : EF Core

app2_1 --> redis : GET/SET
app2_2 --> redis : GET/SET
app2_3 --> redis : GET/SET
app2_4 --> redis : GET/SET

app2_1 --> prom : /metrics endpoint
app2_2 --> prom : /metrics endpoint
app2_3 --> prom : /metrics endpoint
app2_4 --> prom : /metrics endpoint

grafana --> prom : Query metrics
k6_tool --> nginx : HTTP load tests

' =======================
' Connexions Étape 2b
' =======================
krakend --> identity_svc : /api/v1/auth/*\n/api/v1/signup/*
krakend --> wallet_svc : /api/v1/deposits/*
krakend --> marketdata_svc : /api/v1/market-data/*
krakend --> orders_svc : /api/v1/orders/*
krakend --> report_svc : /api/v1/reports/*

nginx3 --> identity_svc : LB
nginx3 --> wallet_svc : LB
nginx3 --> marketdata_svc : LB
nginx3 --> orders_svc : LB
nginx3 --> report_svc : LB

identity_svc --> db_shared : EF Core (identity_db)
wallet_svc --> db_shared : EF Core (wallet_db)
orders_svc --> db_shared : EF Core (orders_db)
marketdata_svc --> db_shared : EF Core (marketdata_db)
report_svc --> db_shared : EF Core (reporting_db)

identity_svc --> redis3 : Session cache
marketdata_svc --> redis3 : Cache quotes (TTL 5s)
orders_svc --> redis3 : Cache orders

orders_svc --> marketdata_svc : Get current prices (pre-trade)
marketdata_svc --> mkt_sim : Stream quotes (WebSocket)
wallet_svc --> pay3 : Process payment
identity_svc --> otp3 : Verify OTP
identity_svc --> kyc3 : Verify KYC

identity_svc --> prom3 : Metrics
wallet_svc --> prom3 : Metrics
orders_svc --> prom3 : Metrics
marketdata_svc --> prom3 : Metrics
report_svc --> prom3 : Metrics

grafana3 --> prom3 : Query

legend right
  **Type de diagramme** : Vue Déploiement (4+1)

  **Architecture en 3 étapes** :
    État initial → Étape 2a (LB/Cache) → Étape 2b (Gateway/Microservices)

  **État initial (Monolith)** :
    Monolith REST simple avec UC-01 (Signup), UC-02 (Auth), UC-03 (Deposits)
    MySQL standalone, simulateurs locaux (otp-sim, kyc-sim, pay-sim)

  **Étape 2a (Observabilité + LB/Cache)** :
    • NGINX load balancer (round-robin, N instances)
    • Redis cache (portfolios, market-data, reports)
    • Prometheus + Grafana (4 Golden Signals)
    • Tests k6 (baseline + scaling)

  **Étape 2b (Gateway + Microservices )** :
    • KrakenD API Gateway (routage, auth, rate limiting, circuit breaker)
    • 5 microservices :
      - Identity :8081 (UC-01, UC-02)
      - Wallet :8082 (UC-03)
      - Market Data :8084 (UC-04 - WebSocket streaming, quotes simulés)
      - Orders :8085 (UC-05 - Place orders, pre-trade checks, matching simulé, P&L)
      - Reporting :8083 (Analytics)
    • MySQL SHARED :3307 (base unique avec schémas séparés)
    • Redis cache spécialisé (sessions, quotes TTL 5s, orders)
    • Communication synchrone REST/HTTP entre services

 
  **Pattern architectural Étape 2b** :
    • Shared Database (avec isolation logique par schéma)
    • Communication synchrone REST/HTTP entre services
    • Cache-aside (Redis pour performance)
    • API Gateway (orchestration, authentification, throttling)
    • Matching et P&L simulés dans Orders Service (pas de Matching Engine externe)
    • Simplicité adaptée au contexte académique

  **Services simulés (internes)** :
    • market-feed-sim : Génère cotations temps réel (UC-04)
    • pay-sim : Règlement dépôts (UC-03)
    • kyc-sim / otp-sim : Vérification identité (UC-01, UC-02)

  **Objectifs NFR (cahier de charges Phase 2)** :
    État initial : Latence P95 ≤500ms, Throughput ≥300 req/s
    Étape 2a : Latence P95 ≤250ms, Throughput ≥800 req/s
    Étape 2b : Latence P95 ≤100ms (UC-05), ≤200ms (UC-04)
end legend

@enduml
